    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d721-a1">

                <pb facs="0829" n="709" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg709"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Republic of Panama National Executive
                    Power.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Office of the Secretary of Government and Foreign Affairs,
                                Department of Foreign Relations</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Panama</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-04-12"><hi rendition="#italic">April 12,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 23.</seg></opener>
                <p>At the request of the Government of the United States of America, made in the
                    name of the Chinese Government, permission is hereby given to the American
                    diplomatic and consular officials to lend their good offices, should they be
                    required, in favor of the Chinese subjects resident on the Isthmus. Communicate
                    to the envoy extraordinary and minister plenipotentiary of the United States in
                    this capital as the result of his esteemed note of the 7th instant, as also to
                    the governors for the information of the authorities within their jurisdiction.
                    Copy and publish.</p>
                <p>Sealed by His Excellency the President.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Santiago de la Guardia</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">The Secretary of Government and Foreign
                            Relations.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
